@page "/theming"
@implements IDisposable
@inject DocsJs Js

<DocShell Title="Theming" Description="@G.Summary" Tracks="G.Tracks" Trail="G.Trail" Portrait="Portrait" PortraitCaption="@($"Active theme · {Current}")">
    <Lede>
        DaisyBlazor uses daisyUI themes. Set <code>data-theme</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> and every semantic colour token swaps,
        so components re-skin automatically. <code>ThemeProvider</code> does it for you, with dark mode and persistence.
    </Lede>
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="prose-doc">
            <p>
                A theme is selected by setting <code>data-theme="..."</code> on the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element; daisyUI swaps every
                semantic colour token (<code>--color-primary</code>, <code>--color-base-100</code>, …). Try it in the preview: every page of
                this site re-skins the same way.
            </p>

            @H(0)
            <p>
                <code>ThemeProvider</code> manages the active theme: it applies <code>data-theme</code>, follows the OS light/dark setting
                (including live changes) when the preference is <code>"system"</code>, and persists the choice to <code>localStorage</code>
                and a cookie. It cascades itself, so descendants can read the state and switch themes. Its JavaScript is a static ES module
                (no <code>eval</code>), so it works under a strict Content-Security-Policy.
            </p>
            <CodeBlock Code="@Wrap" />

            @H(1)
            <p>
                Add the pre-paint script to <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> in <code>App.razor</code>, after <code>&lt;base href&gt;</code>. It is a
                plain static file (no inline code), runs before first paint, and works on static SSR pages that have no circuit:
            </p>
            <CodeBlock Language="xml" Title="App.razor" Code="@InitScript" />
            <p>
                It reads the same <code>localStorage</code> key as <code>ThemeProvider</code> and falls back to
                <code>prefers-color-scheme</code>. If you changed the provider's defaults, mirror them on the tag:
                <code>data-storage-key="..."</code>, <code>data-light="mybrand"</code>, <code>data-dark="mybrand-dark"</code>.
            </p>
            <p>
                By default a stored value is applied as-is. Add <code>data-themes</code> (space- or comma-separated, the same list as the
                provider's <code>Themes</code>) to ignore a stale or unknown stored name and fall back to the light/dark default instead.
                <code>ThemeProvider</code> does the same for names outside <code>Themes</code>:
            </p>
            <CodeBlock Language="xml" Title="App.razor" Code="@InitScriptThemes" />

            @H(2)
            <p>The provider is brand-neutral and parameter-driven: every theme name is configurable.</p>
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>SystemLightTheme</code></td><td><code>"light"</code></td><td>Theme used for <code>"system"</code> in OS light mode.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>SystemDarkTheme</code></td><td><code>"dark"</code></td><td>Theme used for <code>"system"</code> in OS dark mode.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Themes</code></td><td>all 35 built-in daisyUI themes</td><td>The selectable set (e.g. for a picker).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>DarkThemes</code></td><td>daisyUI's dark themes</td><td>Which themes count as "dark" for <code>IsDarkMode</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>StorageKey</code> / <code>CookieKey</code> / <code>DarkModeCookieKey</code></td><td><code>daisy-theme</code> / <code>daisy-theme</code> / <code>daisy-darkmode</code></td><td>Persistence keys.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>InitialPreference</code></td><td><code>null</code></td><td>Seed from the server cookie during SSR to avoid a flash.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>OnThemeChanged</code></td><td>—</td><td>Raised with the resolved theme after a switch.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ThemeChanged</code> (event)</td><td>—</td><td>Raised on every change; subscribe to refresh a component (see below).</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            @H(3)
            <p>
                The cascade is fixed (<code>IsFixed="true"</code>), so a theme change never re-renders the wrapped tree. Components that
                <em>display</em> theme state subscribe to <code>ThemeChanged</code>:
            </p>
            <CodeBlock Code="@Reading" />
            <p>
                <code>Theme.Preference</code> is the stored choice (a theme name or <code>"system"</code>); <code>Theme.Theme</code> is the
                concrete applied theme; <code>Theme.IsDarkMode</code> resolves against <code>DarkThemes</code>. Right now on this page:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><code>Preference</code> = <code>@(Provider?.Preference ?? "—")</code></li>
                <li><code>Theme</code> = <code>@Current</code></li>
                <li><code>IsDarkMode</code> = <code>@((Provider?.IsDarkMode ?? false) ? "true" : "false")</code></li>
            </ul>

            @H(4)
            <p>
                All 35 daisyUI v5 themes are enabled by <code>preset.css</code> (<code>light</code>, <code>dark</code>, <code>cupcake</code>,
                <code>synthwave</code>, <code>dracula</code>, <code>nord</code>, <code>business</code>, <code>night</code>, <code>dim</code>,
                <code>sunset</code>, <code>abyss</code>, <code>silk</code>, …) plus the neutral DaisyBlazor defaults: <strong><code>daisyblazor</code></strong>
                (light, default) and <strong><code>daisyblazor-dark</code></strong> (dark, <code>prefers-color-scheme: dark</code>). To ship only
                the two DaisyBlazor themes, import <code>preset-core.css</code> instead of <code>preset.css</code> (see
                <a href="css-preset">CSS preset</a>). See them all side by side in <a href="themes">the theme gallery</a>.
            </p>

            @H(5)
            <p>Add a daisyUI theme block to your <code>main.css</code> after the preset import, then point <code>ThemeProvider</code> at it:</p>
            <CodeBlock Language="css" Title="Styles/main.css" Code="@BrandCss" />
            <CodeBlock Code="@BrandProvider" />

            @H(6)
            <p>Build a picker from <code>Themes</code> and <code>SetThemeAsync</code>. This one is live and drives the whole site:</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 flex max-w-[70ch] flex-wrap items-center gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-6">
            <select class="select" aria-label="Theme" @onchange="@(e => Provider!.SetThemeAsync(e.Value!.ToString()!))">
                <option value="system">System</option>
                @foreach (string t in Provider?.Themes ?? [])
                {
                    <option value="@t" selected="@(t == Provider!.Preference)">@t</option>
                }
            </select>
            <Chip Color="Color.Primary" Icon="@((Provider?.IsDarkMode ?? false) ? Icons.Material.Filled.DarkMode : Icons.Material.Filled.LightMode)">@Current</Chip>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-doc mt-5">
            <CodeBlock Code="@Picker" />
            <p>
                daisyUI's pure-CSS <code>theme-controller</code> input is also wrapped as the <code>ThemeController</code> component for
                no-JS toggles.
            </p>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
</DocShell>

@code {
    private static readonly GuideDoc G = Guides.Get("theming");
    private static readonly string[] PreviewThemes = ["daisyblazor", "daisyblazor-dark", "retro", "synthwave", "cupcake", "dracula"];

    [CascadingParameter] public ThemeProvider? Provider { get; set; }

    private string Current => Provider?.Theme ?? ThemeDeck.Light;

    private static RenderFragment H(int i) => __builder =>
    {
        <h2 id="@G.Tracks[i].Id" class="scroll-mt-6 font-display">@G.Tracks[i].Title</h2>
    };

    private RenderFragment Portrait => __builder =>
    {
        <div class="space-y-4">
            <div>
                <span class="block truncate font-display text-3xl font-bold leading-tight">@Current</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2">
                @foreach (string t in PreviewThemes)
                {
                    string theme = t;
                    <button type="button" data-theme="@theme" @onclick="e => Apply(theme, e)"
                            aria-pressed="@(theme == Current ? "true" : "false")" title="@theme"
                            class="flex aspect-square flex-col justify-between rounded-md bg-primary p-2 text-left text-primary-content transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 @(theme == Current ? "ring-4 ring-base-content ring-offset-2 ring-offset-base-100" : "")">
                        <span class="size-4 rounded-full bg-secondary"></span>
                        <span class="truncate text-[0.7rem] font-bold">@theme</span>
                    </button>
                }
            </div>
            <ProgressLinear Color="Color.Tertiary" Value="@(100 * ThemeDeck.Number(Current) / ThemeDeck.Themes.Count)" />
        </div>
    };

    private async Task Apply(string theme, MouseEventArgs e)
    {
        if (Provider is null) return;
        await ThemeDeck.PutOnAsync(Provider, Js, theme, e.ClientX, e.ClientY);
    }

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        if (Provider is not null) Provider.ThemeChanged += Refresh;
    }

    private void Refresh() => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    public void Dispose()
    {
        if (Provider is not null) Provider.ThemeChanged -= Refresh;
    }

    private const string Wrap = """
        <ThemeProvider>
            @Body
        </ThemeProvider>
        """;

    private const string InitScript = """
        <script src="_content/DaisyBlazor.Components/theme-init.js"></script>
        """;

    private const string InitScriptThemes = """
        <script src="_content/DaisyBlazor.Components/theme-init.js"
                data-light="mybrand" data-dark="daisyblazor-dark"
                data-themes="mybrand daisyblazor-dark light dark synthwave"></script>
        """;

    private const string Reading = """
        @implements IDisposable

        @code {
            [CascadingParameter] private ThemeProvider? Theme { get; set; }

            protected override void OnInitialized()
            {
                if (Theme is not null) Theme.ThemeChanged += Refresh;
            }

            private void Refresh() => _ = InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

            public void Dispose()
            {
                if (Theme is not null) Theme.ThemeChanged -= Refresh;
            }

            private async Task UseDark() => await Theme!.SetThemeAsync("dark");
            private bool IsDark => Theme?.IsDarkMode ?? false;
        }
        """;

    private const string BrandCss = """
        @import "tailwindcss";
        @import "../obj/daisyblazor/preset.css";

        @plugin "../obj/daisyblazor/daisyui-theme.mjs" {
            name: "mybrand";
            default: true;
            color-scheme: light;
            --color-primary: oklch(55% 0.2 264);
            --color-secondary: oklch(60% 0.18 200);
            /* …base/accent/neutral/info/success/warning/error… */
            --radius-box: 0.75rem;
        }
        """;

    private const string BrandProvider = """
        <ThemeProvider SystemLightTheme="mybrand"
                       SystemDarkTheme="daisyblazor-dark"
                       Themes="@(new[] { "mybrand", "daisyblazor-dark", "light", "dark", "synthwave" })">
            @Body
        </ThemeProvider>
        """;

    private const string Picker = """
        <select class="select" @onchange="@(e => Theme!.SetThemeAsync(e.Value!.ToString()!))">
            <option value="system">System</option>
            @foreach (string t in Theme!.Themes)
            {
                <option value="@t" selected="@(t == Theme.Preference)">@t</option>
            }
        </select>
        """;
}
